---
/**
 * medicaid/index.astro
 * Medicaid & Savings Programs hub.
 */

import SectionLayout from '@layouts/SectionLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const allArticles = await getCollection('medicaid', ({ data }) => {
  return data.draft !== true;
});

const sortedArticles = allArticles.sort((a, b) => {
  return new Date(b.data.publishDate).getTime() - new Date(a.data.publishDate).getTime();
});

const articlesList = sortedArticles.map(art => ({
  title: art.data.title,
  description: art.data.description,
  href: `/medicaid/${art.id}/`,
  publishDate: art.data.publishDate
}));

const toolsList = [
  {
    title: 'Medicare Savings Programs (MSP) Eligibility Estimator',
    description: 'Find out if your income qualifies you for state Medicaid assistance (QMB, SLMB, QI) to pay your Medicare Part B premiums and copayments.',
    href: '/tools/medicare-savings-estimator/'
  },
  {
    title: 'SNAP Eligibility Calculator for Seniors',
    description: 'Estimate your monthly food assistance (Food Stamps) benefit under special senior income and excess medical expense deduction rules.',
    href: '/tools/snap-eligibility-calculator-for-seniors/'
  },
  {
    title: 'LIHEAP Heating & Cooling Assistance Checker',
    description: 'See if you qualify for state Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Program (LIHEAP) grants to pay winter heating or summer cooling bills.',
    href: '/tools/liheap-eligibility-checker/'
  },
  {
    title: 'Extra Help (Part D Low-Income Subsidy) Calculator',
    description: 'Check if you qualify for federal Extra Help to lower your Medicare Part D prescription drug premiums, deductibles, and copays to near zero.',
    href: '/tools/extra-help-eligibility-calculator/'
  },
  {
    title: 'Universal Senior Benefits Screener',
    description: 'Answer simple questions to screen your eligibility across Medicare Savings, SNAP, LIHEAP, property tax relief, and prescription assistance simultaneously.',
    href: '/tools/universal-senior-benefits-screener/'
  }
];
const medicaidIntro = `
<h2>Medicaid and Low-Income Benefits for Seniors: What the Programs Actually Cover</h2>
<p>
  Many seniors assume Medicaid is only for people living in nursing homes or for those who are extremely poor.
  In reality, a range of federal and state programs built on the Medicaid framework help millions of older
  Americans pay Medicare premiums, prescription drug costs, utility bills, and grocery expenses — programs
  that most eligible seniors never know to apply for.
</p>

<h2>Medicare Savings Programs: The Most Underclaimed Benefit</h2>
<p>
  Medicare Savings Programs (MSPs) are state-run Medicaid programs that pay some or all of your Medicare
  out-of-pocket costs if your income falls below federal guidelines. The four program tiers — QMB, SLMB, QI,
  and QDWI — cover different combinations of Part A premiums, Part B premiums, deductibles, and copayments.
</p>
<p>
  In 2026, a single person with monthly income below approximately \$1,695 may qualify for at least partial
  help. Yet CMS and SSA data consistently show that several million eligible seniors are not enrolled. The
  main barrier is awareness. Use our
  <a href="/tools/medicare-savings-estimator/">Medicare Savings Program Eligibility Estimator</a> to check
  whether your income qualifies.
</p>

<h2>Extra Help (Low-Income Subsidy): Near-Zero Drug Costs</h2>
<p>
  Seniors who qualify for a Medicare Savings Program automatically qualify for Extra Help — a federal subsidy
  that reduces Medicare Part D drug costs to near zero. In 2026, Extra Help beneficiaries pay no more than
  \$4.50 for generic drugs and \$11.20 for brand-name drugs per prescription, with no deductible or coverage gap.
  If you are currently enrolled in a Medicare Savings Program and paying full drug copays, contact 1-800-MEDICARE
  to ensure your Extra Help has been applied.
</p>

<h2>SNAP: Food Benefits for Seniors</h2>
<p>
  The Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP) has special eligibility rules for households where at
  least one member is 60 or older. Seniors can deduct excess medical expenses from their income calculation —
  meaning that high prescription drug costs or regular medical transportation may make you eligible even if
  your gross income is above the standard limit. Use our
  <a href="/tools/snap-eligibility-calculator-for-seniors/">SNAP Eligibility Calculator for Seniors</a> to
  run the numbers for your household.
</p>

<h2>LIHEAP: Help With Heating and Cooling Bills</h2>
<p>
  The Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program (LIHEAP) provides federal grants — administered by states —
  to help low-income households pay winter heating and summer cooling bills. Because seniors on fixed incomes
  are disproportionately affected by energy cost spikes, LIHEAP prioritizes households where a member is 60
  or older. Check your eligibility with our
  <a href="/tools/liheap-eligibility-checker/">LIHEAP Eligibility Checker</a>.
</p>
`;
---

<SectionLayout
  title="Medicaid Eligibility Guides for Seniors"
  description="Learn state Medicaid guidelines for seniors, asset limit rules, nursing home coverage, and federal assistance to pay Medicare out-of-pocket costs."
  intro={medicaidIntro}
  tools={toolsList}
  articles={articlesList}
/>
